1
00:00:09,161 --> 00:00:13,252
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:14,742 --> 00:00:15,915
Yeah...

3
00:00:15,915 --> 00:00:19,983
I'm about 95% sure this
scientist didn't kill himself

4
00:00:19,983 --> 00:00:24,451
to paint the floor with his own blood as
part of a performance art piece he was doing.

5
00:00:24,451 --> 00:00:27,529
Even Engineering wouldn't
do something like that.

6
00:00:27,529 --> 00:00:28,250
The hell with it;

7
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:33,094
if I turned around every time I saw a
dead body and a huge blood trail...

8
00:00:33,094 --> 00:00:35,375
well, I'd probably be
a lot safer right now

9
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:38,567
but I wouldn't be any closer to
getting out of here, so...

10
00:00:38,567 --> 00:00:40,049
Yeah, damn!

11
00:00:40,049 --> 00:00:44,854
I'm not a crime scene specialist
but I think we can rule out nosebleed.

12
00:00:44,854 --> 00:00:47,254
Well, maybe, if he sneezed there...

13
00:00:47,254 --> 00:00:49,857
...no. No.

14
00:00:49,857 --> 00:00:52,233
Well, I don't see any
casings or bullet holes,

15
00:00:52,233 --> 00:00:53,381
so what was the cause of--

16
00:00:53,381 --> 00:00:54,599
[gunshots]

17
00:00:54,599 --> 00:00:55,655
NINJAS!

18
00:00:55,655 --> 00:00:58,203
Dammit, of course! That's
like rule number 1!

19
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:05,786
It's Occam's Shuriken! When the answer
is elusive, never rule out ninjas!

20
00:01:05,786 --> 00:01:06,463
Where are they?

21
00:01:06,463 --> 00:01:07,659
[gunshots]
Shit.

22
00:01:08,278 --> 00:01:09,496
Where are they coming from?

23
00:01:09,496 --> 00:01:10,822
[gunshots]
[screaming]

24
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:16,849
See? That one dropped in from
nowhere; I should expect that!

25
00:01:16,849 --> 00:01:20,532
But, at the same time, I can't
expect that because they're ninjas.

26
00:01:20,532 --> 00:01:23,091
As soon as I expect it,
they won't do it.

27
00:01:23,091 --> 00:01:26,995
Ninjas understand quantum
mechanics better than people realize.

28
00:01:26,995 --> 00:01:29,999
That was a controversial part
of my dissertation.

29
00:01:29,999 --> 00:01:31,791
Shit, is that all of them?

30
00:01:31,791 --> 00:01:33,694
Truly, I'll never know.

31
00:01:33,694 --> 00:01:35,460
Science is no help here.

32
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:39,901
You can never prove the absence
of ninjas, only their direct presence.

33
00:01:39,901 --> 00:01:42,147
Oh, this must be how they're
getting in here.

34
00:01:42,147 --> 00:01:44,103
Hell, if I can climb this, so can a...

35
00:01:45,163 --> 00:01:45,976
...ninja.

36
00:01:45,976 --> 00:01:52,006
This also confirms what I saw yesterday
was real because I thought I saw ninjas,

37
00:01:52,006 --> 00:01:56,655
but that was kind of fuzzy in my head,
but here they are, without a doubt.

38
00:01:56,655 --> 00:02:00,968
I need to stop doubting my own
sanity because I'm still right about

39
00:02:00,968 --> 00:02:01,645
[gunshots]
EVERYTHING!

40
00:02:02,479 --> 00:02:04,849
Oh, my God, did I hit that one?

41
00:02:06,679 --> 00:02:07,620
Shit!

42
00:02:09,508 --> 00:02:10,911
DAMN, YOU'RE SPOOKY!

43
00:02:12,703 --> 00:02:16,498
Yeah, you can't double-back on
ninjas. You have to triple-back.

44
00:02:16,498 --> 00:02:17,037
YAH!

45
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:18,601
Woo-HYAH!

46
00:02:18,601 --> 00:02:22,243
I can't even really be sure if the
ninjas I've shot are actually dead.

47
00:02:22,243 --> 00:02:23,994
They could just be faking it.

48
00:02:23,994 --> 00:02:28,604
They don't seem have much armor so they can't
take the 12-gauge, but the 9 millimeter?

49
00:02:28,604 --> 00:02:29,184
[gunshots]
I d--

50
00:02:29,184 --> 00:02:30,114
AAAH!

51
00:02:30,114 --> 00:02:32,206
JESUS CHRIST!

52
00:02:32,206 --> 00:02:34,642
I can NOT be too careful!

53
00:02:34,642 --> 00:02:35,783
And I'm not!

54
00:02:36,412 --> 00:02:39,196
But, yeah, I remember reading
about those Colombian drug lords

55
00:02:39,196 --> 00:02:42,936
buying designer clothes that were
bulletproof against low-caliber shots.

56
00:02:42,936 --> 00:02:44,680
Eh, not this way.

57
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,424
So, it wouldn't surprise me one bit

58
00:02:46,424 --> 00:02:49,364
if ninja suits had something
similar woven into them.

59
00:02:49,364 --> 00:02:53,130
Y'know, I'm going to freak out if I
come back and all the bodies are gone.

60
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:54,468
Okay, that's one...

61
00:02:55,563 --> 00:02:57,773
Any more ninjas...?

62
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:02,266
There's two.

63
00:03:02,266 --> 00:03:05,835
Now, I don't get it. They seem
to be wearing night-vision goggles.

64
00:03:05,835 --> 00:03:10,689
If I was a ninja, like a legit one,
I would start shooting out the lights.

65
00:03:10,689 --> 00:03:13,285
That would be a big advantage.

66
00:03:13,285 --> 00:03:15,573
But, I'm not going to tell
them how to do their job.

67
00:03:16,155 --> 00:03:19,187
Death can be a learning experience.

68
00:03:19,187 --> 00:03:23,217
But, really, in all likelihood,
this is how I'm going to die.

69
00:03:23,217 --> 00:03:27,298
Not today, I'm strapped and
wired as shit right now,

70
00:03:27,298 --> 00:03:30,782
but hey, maybe a year
from now-- ten years--

71
00:03:30,782 --> 00:03:35,081
it's almost a certainty ninjas are going
to track me down and try and kill me.

72
00:03:35,081 --> 00:03:36,966
It's a matter of honor now.

73
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:37,437
Ha!

74
00:03:38,691 --> 00:03:43,635
And, really, it's no surprise, given
my lifestyle. I'd hardly be the first.

75
00:03:43,635 --> 00:03:44,592
[lock jiggles]

76
00:03:44,592 --> 00:03:46,004
Who's the Italian one?

77
00:03:46,004 --> 00:03:51,686
Ettore Majorana. Brilliant theoretical
physicist, friends with Heisenberg,

78
00:03:51,686 --> 00:03:54,574
wasn't much older than me before
he was killed by ninjas.

79
00:03:55,212 --> 00:03:56,136
[agrunts growl]
[screaming]

80
00:03:56,136 --> 00:03:58,445
[hivehand fires]
YOU'RE NOT A NINJA! STOP PRETENDING!

81
00:03:58,787 --> 00:03:59,861
OW!

82
00:04:01,114 --> 00:04:02,842
WAAAAAAAAAAAAAAH!

83
00:04:04,843 --> 00:04:08,430
DAMMIT! YOU TRICKED ME INTO
KILLING YOU IN A REALLY LOUD WAY!

84
00:04:10,472 --> 00:04:12,336
[agrunt moans]

85
00:04:12,336 --> 00:04:15,749
OH, WHAT ARE YOU COMPLAINING
ABOUT? YOU HAVE A HELMET!

86
00:04:15,749 --> 00:04:19,995
This is bullshit! We need to nuke this
whole place as soon as I'm out.

87
00:04:19,995 --> 00:04:20,924
God dammit...

88
00:04:26,854 --> 00:04:30,602
Christ, I'm running light on bullets
because every one of you bastards

89
00:04:30,602 --> 00:04:34,191
are built like... jacked-up
space bouncers!

90
00:04:34,191 --> 00:04:37,103
I'm starting to think your species
communicates only through

91
00:04:37,103 --> 00:04:40,001
a series of body lifts and squat thrusts.

92
00:04:40,001 --> 00:04:43,353
Oh, what the fuck is that?! SOMEBODY
ELSE TRYING TO TAKE A SHOT AT ME?!

93
00:04:43,353 --> 00:04:44,203
HERE YOU GO!

94
00:04:44,773 --> 00:04:46,203
[explosion]

95
00:04:46,203 --> 00:04:48,051
Aahh... damn...

96
00:04:48,051 --> 00:04:50,984
I kind of botched that. Stupid railing.

97
00:04:50,984 --> 00:04:52,357
Are they still there?

98
00:04:55,198 --> 00:04:57,682
Well, I woke them up at the very least.

99
00:04:57,682 --> 00:05:01,463
I should move in for a closer shot
while they... meditate... or...

100
00:05:02,049 --> 00:05:03,075
I-I don't know what they're doing.

101
00:05:03,075 --> 00:05:04,991
AAAH!
SCIENTIST: I apologize, Mr. Freeman,

102
00:05:04,991 --> 00:05:08,280
SCIENTIST: but I couldn't risk opening that
door until I was sure you had scoured the area.

103
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,221
IT'S YOU!

104
00:05:09,221 --> 00:05:11,409
SCIENTIST: This is the last
entrance to the Lambda Complex.

105
00:05:11,409 --> 00:05:13,872
SCIENTIST: Every other has been
sealed off to contain the invasion.

106
00:05:13,872 --> 00:05:14,975
That won't work.

107
00:05:14,975 --> 00:05:17,009
SCIENTIST: When we realized that
you might actually make it here

108
00:05:17,009 --> 00:05:20,322
SCIENTIST: we drew straws to see who
should stay behind to let you through.

109
00:05:20,322 --> 00:05:22,009
SCIENTIST: Obviously, I
drew the short one.

110
00:05:22,009 --> 00:05:23,921
Okay, okay, I won't kill you.

111
00:05:23,921 --> 00:05:26,954
SCIENTIST: ...tip of the Lambda
Reactor. Waiting for YOU, I mean.

112
00:05:26,954 --> 00:05:27,485
What?

113
00:05:27,485 --> 00:05:29,464
SCIENTIST: The reactor is shut
down right now,

114
00:05:29,464 --> 00:05:31,033
SCIENTIST: but you can activate
it on your way up.

115
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:31,421
No!

116
00:05:31,421 --> 00:05:34,483
SCIENTIST: You'll have to flood the core
anyway to get into the Teleportation Labs.

117
00:05:34,483 --> 00:05:35,134
Teleportat--?

118
00:05:35,134 --> 00:05:37,533
SCIENTIST: You're not authorized
to know about those,

119
00:05:37,533 --> 00:05:41,668
SCIENTIST: but I can see you already know a
great deal more than any one man is supposed to.

120
00:05:41,668 --> 00:05:43,614
Yeah, story of my life.

121
00:05:43,614 --> 00:05:46,345
What the hell are you talking
about Teleportation "Labs"?

122
00:05:46,345 --> 00:05:48,583
Do we have a room to study this already?

123
00:05:48,583 --> 00:05:49,408
Is this it?

124
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,658
No...

125
00:05:51,658 --> 00:05:55,057
Okay, well, first off, that
containment shit isn't going to work.

126
00:05:55,057 --> 00:05:57,492
They're teleporting. We need to leave!

127
00:05:58,348 --> 00:05:59,871
PA: Access denied.

128
00:05:59,871 --> 00:06:01,588
Hey, your thing's broken.

129
00:06:01,588 --> 00:06:03,201
Yeah, you take a look at it.

130
00:06:03,201 --> 00:06:07,799
But, seriously, how are you going to
seal off monsters teleporting in from the air?

131
00:06:07,799 --> 00:06:11,300
You think if you deadbolt the
door that'll do it. You're safe?

132
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:15,050
And what was all that crap about
a reactor and flooding it or something?

133
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:18,235
Everyone here is talking like
I've missed some sort of briefing.

134
00:06:18,235 --> 00:06:19,806
SCIENTIST: Were you in
Weapons Research, too?

135
00:06:19,806 --> 00:06:20,506
...sure.

136
00:06:20,506 --> 00:06:22,260
SCIENTIST: I built the gluon gun,

137
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:25,912
SCIENTIST: but I just can't bring
myself to use it on a living creature.

138
00:06:25,912 --> 00:06:28,039
SCIENTIST: You don't look as if
you have any trouble killing things.

139
00:06:28,039 --> 00:06:31,139
Yeah, this blood's not coming off, is it?

140
00:06:31,587 --> 00:06:34,868
So, what did you say this was?
A prototype leaf-blower?

141
00:06:34,868 --> 00:06:39,043
I don't know, man, this thing's pretty
heavy, and I'm already carrying a load.

142
00:06:39,043 --> 00:06:40,908
I may not be able to haul this too far.

143
00:06:42,291 --> 00:06:44,872
Nice! Looks like plasma.

144
00:06:44,872 --> 00:06:46,352
Okay, I'll try it.

145
00:06:46,352 --> 00:06:47,711
Is this the ammo?

146
00:06:47,711 --> 00:06:49,386
Well, as long as it's sealed.

147
00:06:49,969 --> 00:06:51,765
So, uh, hey, what's this do?

148
00:06:52,627 --> 00:06:54,308
Oh, shit! I need to conserve ammo!

149
00:06:54,308 --> 00:06:55,614
[scientist screaming]
I'M NOT DEALING WITH THIS!

150
00:06:55,614 --> 00:06:55,928
SCIENTIST: NO!

151
00:06:55,928 --> 00:06:58,207
YOU HANDLE IT! YOUR LAB, YOUR RULES!

152
00:06:58,207 --> 00:06:59,196
[scientist screaming]

153
00:06:59,196 --> 00:07:00,149
BYE!

154
00:07:02,744 --> 00:07:06,726
Sometimes, I wonder... if I
could've done things differently...

